     "result_text_tail": "s cash excludes stock, because the pack doesn't give a figure for it.\n- **Duty timing:** the duty case assumes the 25% rate applies from January 2028.\n- **Trade-press figure left out:** the $5.2B \"US K-beauty market\" figure also counts makeup and hair care, so the deck uses the $3.6B skincare figure and says why in a footnote.\n\n**Checks**\n- **No gaps:** all 217 numbers come from the briefing pack or a calculation on it, and none are placeholders.\n- **QA:** the checker passes with 0 failures and 4 warnings, all minor:\n  - The three annual growth rates (CAGRs) need a power, which the source workbook's formula format can't express, so they show the formula as text rather than a live calculation.\n  - One figure beside the payback chart (cash effect per point of ad cost) is flagged because it explains the gaps between the bars rather than being read off them.\n- **Layout:** the renderer reports no layout problems. I couldn't look at the slides as images because LibreOffice isn't installed, so a quick visual pass in PowerPoint is worth doing.\n- **No source re-check run:** there are no web sources, so the step that re-opens sources online didn't apply.\n\nFrom here I can switch the theme, add a separate stress test on volume, or make the 28% pilot ad cost the base case throughout instead of the planning team's 25%.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- onsoo-us-entry.pptx\n- onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx \u2014 every number, its source and live formulas\n- onsoo-us-entry.json \u2014 the spec, to re-render"
